WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:03.480
What happens when the Lockes come face to
face with their new foe?

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.940
And will Tyler return home to help his family?

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:10.280
Here's what you need to know before you watch
the final season of "Locke and Key."

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.760
Season 3 of "Locke &amp; Key" has been in production
for quite some time, and it had actually been

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.059
written before Season 2 even premiered.

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:18.480
Producer Carlton Cuse explained to Collider,

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.060
"It was actually a really weird thing that
I've never experienced in my career, to have

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.480
written a full season of television that hadn't
been made, and we had to go on to writing

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.410
the next season of television."

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:31.470
Season 3 was also shot back to back with Season
2, meaning that filming wrapped in September

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.570
2021, a month before Season 2 hit Netflix.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:38.269
Connor Jessup, who plays Tyler Locke on the
show, posted a series of behind-the-scenes

00:00:38.269 --> 00:00:40.010
snaps on Instagram, and wrote,

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.399
"that's a wrap on season 3 of locke &amp; key.

00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:43.780
after a year of shooting, we're done.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:46.559
I'm a tangled mess [...] I'm sleepy and happy
and sad.

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:47.719
but mostly, I'm grateful.

00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:50.639
it's been a weird, sh—- year and this show
has been a refuge."

00:00:50.639 --> 00:00:55.760
Thankfully, fans won't have to wait too long
for Netflix to drop Season 3.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.100
Netflix has been teasing "Locke and Key" Season
3 on social media since the end of 2021, but

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:03.059
has been cagey with release details until
now.

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:07.090
During Netflix's Geeked Week event, the streamer
shared a trailer for Season 3 and revealed

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:10.039
that the series will return on August 10,
2022.

00:01:10.039 --> 00:01:14.920
"Locke &amp; Key" Season 3 will air a mere 10
months after Season 2, compared to the 20-month

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.840
wait fans endured between the first and second
seasons.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:22.000
This highly anticipated season will reportedly
consist of eight episodes, which is a departure

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.950
from the previous 10-episode format.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:28.049
Hopefully, this shorter season is still able
to mirror the success of the previous season,

00:01:28.049 --> 00:01:32.530
which was streamed for more than 143 million
hours globally during its first four weeks

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:34.740
on Netflix.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:38.189
Now that Netflix has announced the release
date for Season 3, fans are clamoring to know

00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:42.049
if their favorite characters will return for
the next installment of "Locke and Key."

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:45.460
Thankfully, most of the show's main actors
have confirmed they'll be returning.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:48.929
Connor Jessup was one of the first actors
to reaffirm his place in the series, even

00:01:48.929 --> 00:01:52.499
though his character Tyler Locke leaves to
go traveling at the end of Season 2.

00:01:52.499 --> 00:01:54.619
Jessup told Decider in October 2021,

00:01:54.619 --> 00:01:58.899
"I don't think when he leaves at the end of
Season 2 that his story is over [...] To me,

00:01:58.899 --> 00:02:01.560
it felt like a new chapter, but it didn't
feel like a resolution.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.479
So, there's still more for Tyler."

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:07.479
Jessup will be joined by Emilia Jones and
Jackson Robert Scott, who play his younger

00:02:07.479 --> 00:02:09.110
siblings, Kinsey and Bode.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:13.400
Darby Stanchfield will also be returning as
their mom, Nina Locke, along with Aaron Ashmore,

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.470
who plays Duncan, the Locke childrens' uncle.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:19.790
Meanwhile, Sherri Saum, who plays Ellie, has
been promoted to series regular, which means

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:23.180
we might also see more of Coby Bird, who plays
her son Rufus.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:27.540
Kevin Durand will also be getting more screen
time as the Revolutionary War soldier Captain

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.489
Frederick Gideon.

00:02:29.489 --> 00:02:33.530
The dramatic second season of "Locke &amp; Key"
came to a conclusion at the same time as Matheson

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:34.709
Academy's fall semester.

00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:38.680
At the end of the season finale, Nina reveals
that Tyler is going traveling over the winter

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.580
break because he needs a fresh start.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:45.020
However, the trailer for Season 3 places Tyler
squarely in the middle of all the action alongside

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:49.150
his family, so viewers can expect some time
to have elapsed between the second and third

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:50.150
seasons.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:53.530
This means that the earliest the series could
be set is the beginning of the spring semester,

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.920
with Tyler returning to finish his education.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.540
However, it's also possible that more time
has passed, taking viewers to the end of the

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.819
summer semester and Tyler's last few weeks
at Matheson Academy.

00:03:02.819 --> 00:03:06.629
Alternatively, there could be less of a school
focus this season and the show could be set

00:03:06.629 --> 00:03:10.610
entirely during the summer holidays, giving
the Locke family plenty of time to deal with

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:13.250
the show's latest villain.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:17.290
For the last two seasons, "Locke &amp; Key" has
had a revolving door of villains and antagonists.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:22.069
However, in Season 3, Tyler, Kinsey, Bode,
Nina, and Duncan will be facing a new villain,

00:03:22.069 --> 00:03:23.239
and that's Frederick Gideon.

00:03:23.239 --> 00:03:25.459
"Who the hell are you?"

00:03:25.459 --> 00:03:26.829
"Your captain."

00:03:26.829 --> 00:03:31.160
This Revolutionary War captain played by Kevin
Durand made his debut in flashbacks seen during

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.840
the first episode of Season 2.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:36.959
He appeared in a total of four episodes, which
explain his backstory and how a demon took

00:03:36.959 --> 00:03:39.920
over his body when he found the Black Door
in the sea caves.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:44.180
In the last episode of Season 2, the demon
inhabiting Eden's body brought Captain Gideon

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:49.019
back as an echo, initially unaware that a
demon was also inhabiting his body.

00:03:49.019 --> 00:03:52.689
After throwing Eden into the well, Gideon
left with the Anywhere Key.

00:03:52.689 --> 00:03:56.260
During a roundtable interview, showrunner
Carlton Cuse explained that Durand's character

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.980
will be a deadly threat to the Locke family,
saying,

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:02.260
"Meredith and I were faced with the challenge
of how [do] we up the stakes [...] and come

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.870
up with a source of villainy that would feel
like an escalation and also be compelling.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:10.030
That led us to create this character of Gideon
and Kevin seemed like the perfect guy to play

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:11.030
him."

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:14.959
One of the biggest changes going into Season
3 of "Locke &amp; Key" is that Tyler has no memory

00:04:14.959 --> 00:04:17.959
of the magic he and his siblings discovered
at Keyhouse.

00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:20.760
In the final episode of Season 2, Tyler leaves
to go traveling.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.070
"The past is always with us.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:26.360
You can try to run away."

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:30.420
He plans to return after his 18th birthday
with no memory of magic, despite having spent

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:34.080
most of the season searching for the Memory
Key, which would allow him to remember magic

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.200
as an adult.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.890
Instead, he tells his siblings that he wants
to live a normal life after his birthday and

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:40.950
opts not to remember magic.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:44.760
After all, magic caused the death of his dad
and his girlfriend, becoming a major source

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.710
of emotional trauma for him.

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:49.290
"I want to have a normal life."

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:53.360
However, it seems like a magic-free life might
not be in the cards for Tyler, especially

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.640
with Captain Gideon lurking in the shadows.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.440
And Tyler certainly appears to have his memories
back in the trailer.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:02.020
"Locke &amp; Key" has always been a very family-oriented
show.

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:05.990
However, the events of the Season 2 finale
have seen some significant changes that will

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.670
affect the Locke family dynamic.

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:11.260
Plus, Tyler's bonds with his siblings will
undoubtedly change after he forgets about

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.260
magic.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:15.710
Meanwhile, Nina will probably grow closer
to her children now that she knows about magic,

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:18.960
as it has been a barrier between them in previous
seasons.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:22.730
Essentially, Season 3 will focus on how the
Lockes navigate these changes and come together

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:24.220
to face Captain Gideon.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:26.560
As showrunner Meredith Averill teased to Collider,

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.600
"The third season focuses much more heavily
on the family.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.810
They're gonna face the greatest threat they've
had to face yet.

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:34.050
That really bonds them in a way that we've
never seen before.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.780
I can't say more than that."

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:40.280
Kinsey and Scot finally getting together is
something viewers of the show had been waiting

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:44.280
for, ever since their budding romance was
dashed after Gabe swooped in and grabbed Kinsey's

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.280
attention.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:49.060
Of course, Gabe turned out to be the evil
demon echo Dodge, so that relationship was

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:51.310
pretty much doomed from the start.

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:55.410
As Kinsey started to uncover Gabe's true identity,
she and Scot fell for each other again, but

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:57.440
their timing wasn't great.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:00.940
Season 2 concluded with the couple about to
embark on a long-distance relationship as

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:05.210
Scot chose to attend film school in London
for a year before going to college.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:08.970
However, Scot's nickname for Kinsey is rocky
road, and that could be what the couple are

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:10.780
in for in Season 3.

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:15.000
In fact, Netflix has yet to confirm if Petrice
Jones, who plays Scot, is returning for the

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.550
third season, and he doesn't appear in the
trailer.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:21.220
Other cast members have posted behind-the-scenes
photos from the new season on Instagram, but

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:23.420
Jones is strangely missing from the snaps.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:27.310
That said, it's very possible Jones' return
to the show is just being kept under wraps

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:31.700
for dramatic effect, and Kinsey and Scot will
end up back together in Season 3.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:35.290
"I'm here, you know, if you need me."

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:39.770
While Petrice Jones' return is up in the air,
another Locke love interest is definitely

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.030
due back in Matheson for Season 3.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:45.740
Brendan Hines will once again be featured
as Nina's on-again-off-again partner Josh

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:46.740
Bennett.

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:49.300
The pair left their relationship up in the
air last season.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.970
When Josh told Nina he finally felt able to
move on from his wife's death and commit to

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.030
her properly, she shut him down.

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:58.610
In the season finale, Nina explained that
she wasn't ready, and told him she needed

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:00.370
more time before they could be together.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:04.180
However, they certainly left things open-ended,
with the possibility for their relationship

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:05.810
to blossom in Season 3.

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:09.980
However, if Nina and Josh do rekindle their
romance, the fact that she knows about magic

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:13.880
might make things a bit more difficult for
them going forward.

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:17.870
It's always exciting when a "Locke &amp; Key"
character reveals a new magical key, and thankfully

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.040
there's more excitement to come in Season
3.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.940
Duncan now has the ability to make keys, which
is a good skill to have with a supervillain

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:24.940
on the loose.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:28.770
According to the comics created by Joe Hill,
there are still plenty of keys left for the

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:31.730
Lockes to find and the trailer introduces
a pretty major one.

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:36.160
It looks like Bode discovers the Timeshift
Key, allowing users to see visions of the

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:39.010
past when used in the Lockes' grandfather
clock.

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:42.520
This could certainly come in handy as the
Locke family try to discover more about Captain

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.390
Gideon's past in order to defeat him.

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:48.560
It also might come into play for Tyler when
he gets his memories back, as he could see

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.750
visions of his past self using magic.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:51.940
"This key.

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:56.520
This key can make it so you never forget."

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:00.310
Season 2 also introduced a lot of new keys
to the show, in addition to the ones established

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:01.520
in the first season.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:05.210
Fans are certainly eager to see more keys
like the Angel Key, which Kinsey used in the

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:08.990
finale and was instrumental in helping to
defeat Dodge.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:13.050
Season 3 will be the Locke family's last paranormal
adventure on Netflix.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:16.300
The show hasn't been canceled, though, as
it was always the plan to end the story after

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:17.430
three seasons.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:21.560
According to co-showrunners Carlton Cuse and
Meredith Averill, "Locke &amp; Key" will naturally

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:26.020
reach its conclusion at the end of Season
3, with the duo telling Deadline in a statement,

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:29.720
"Once we began working on the series, we felt
three seasons was the ideal length to bring

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:33.909
the story of the Locke family and their Keyhouse
adventures to a satisfying conclusion."

00:08:33.909 --> 00:08:38.099
They also sang the praises of writer Joe Hill
and illustrator Gabriel Rodriguez, who created

00:08:38.099 --> 00:08:40.379
the "Locke and Key" comic book series, and
joked,

00:08:40.379 --> 00:08:44.330
"We're keeping the magical keys, though, for
our own personal use."

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:47.440
Since Cuse and Averill have been planning
the conclusion of "Locke &amp; Key" since the

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:51.620
end of Season 1, they should have the opportunity
to tie up all of the show's loose threads.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:55.620
So, here's hoping fans get everything they
want to see and more in Season 3 of "Locke

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:57.170
&amp; Key."

00:08:57.170 --> 00:09:00.670
The "Locke &amp; Key" showrunners have been keeping
quiet about a lot of the particulars in the

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:04.920
upcoming season, but the trailer does reveal
a few extra details for fans.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.240
For one, it looks like Gideon is creating
an army.

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:11.610
While his motives aren't clear, the trailer
suggests he's coming for the keys, and possibly

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:13.230
even Keyhouse itself.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:17.850
However, Gideon's evil plans appear to culminate
in a big battle between his army and the Lockes.

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:20.100
"This is our house.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.350
Those keys belong to us."

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:26.290
Viewers can definitely expect to see an epic
showdown as Tyler, Kinsey, Bode, Nina, and

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:30.000
Duncan defend their home and the keys in the
battle to end all battles.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.920
This fight promises to be a satisfying and
dramatic conclusion to the final season of

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:35.560
"Locke &amp; Key."

